that paper reminds me -- possibly you don't need to do a bootstrap if you're interested in the realized N which is just n + E(n0 | y) and so you can use the delta method to get at the variance of the 2nd bit too (the formula might be in that paper....).  I think the bootstrap idea came up in the context of subsets of the statespace maybe.

